  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0: First stable release. The public API and v1 wire format are now under SemVer — held stable since the preview series and committed for 1.0.x. The wire format and public surface are unchanged from 1.0.0-preview.10; a pre-release review added two small hardening fixes (encryption-plaintext zeroing is now exception-safe; oversized-token rejections now emit the failure metric). IMPORTANT — the lack of an independent cryptographic audit is now a PERMANENT, documented limitation rather than a release gate: no third party has reviewed the design or implementation. Ship this only where you control both the issuer and every verifier and accept that risk with eyes open. NOT a drop-in OAuth/OIDC/JWT replacement; tokens do NOT interoperate with generic JWT/JWE tooling (the X-Wing key-management profile is not a standardized JOSE/JWE profile). Vulnerability reporting: GitHub Security Advisories (see SECURITY.md). Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md — known limitations: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-jwt/blob/main/KNOWN-GAPS.md.",
